+// Applies a value from a *configuration* source - the same rank LoadConfig writes at - so an
+// application can layer a file of its own under the game's own config: what is applied first
+// is outranked by a later config write, and a command-line flag or the environment outranks
+// both. Returns false only when the value was rejected (an unknown flag, or one whose
+// constraints refuse the value); a value skipped because a higher-priority source already won
+// returns true. The counterpart of LoadConfig for a config that is not a TOML table the
+// registry can walk key by key.
+bool SetFlagFromConfig(std::string_view name, std::string_view value);
